AxonWall — Debian firewall appliance
====================================

AxonWall is a standalone firewall appliance built on the Debian operating
system. It is assembled from Debian's curated package repositories and wraps
upstream free-software components without forking them.

AxonWall itself does not yet carry a project license file; this notice covers
the third-party components it builds and ships. Component versions and licenses
are recorded in THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES in this directory.

Third-party components
----------------------

AxonWall is built on, and ships, the following third-party works:

- **Debian 13 "trixie"** — the base operating system of both the build
  environment and the appliance. Debian is a registered trademark of Software
  in the Public Interest, Inc. The distribution's packages are released under
  their respective licenses; see THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.
- **Debian live-build** (with live-boot, live-config, live-tools) — the ISO
  image factory. AxonWall wraps it; it is not modified.
- **The shipped daemons and engines** — the Linux kernel, nftables,
  systemd-networkd, dnsmasq, Unbound, WireGuard, OpenSSH, and the rest of the
  curated runtime package set listed in
  build/livebuild/config/package-lists/.

Their copyright statements and license identifiers, as declared in the Debian
repositories, are listed in THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES. Each package's complete
copyright and license text is available on the installed appliance under
/usr/share/doc/<package>/copyright and from the Debian sources at
https://sources.debian.org/.

Non-free firmware
-----------------

The ISO includes a curated subset of hardware firmware packages from Debian's
`non-free-firmware` archive area (Realtek and Intel NIC firmware), required for
appliance hardware to operate. These redistribution-permitted binaries are not
free-software licenses in the DFSG sense; see THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES for the
per-package license statements.
